<title>EGYPT: Egypt says buys 200,000T Australian wheat for $150.</title>
<headline>Egypt says buys 200,000T Australian wheat for $150.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Egyptian state's General Authority for Supply Commodities (GASC) said on Saturday it was buying 200,000 tonnes of Australian standard soft white wheat from the Australian Wheat Board for $150 FOB.</p>
<p>GASC vice chairman Samir Shakankiri told Reuters loading was December 11 to 31.</p>
<p>-- Christine Hauser +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
